    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but the examples you gave feel a bit different. those were massive, state-funded projects with specific missions. ai is a bit different, isn't it? it's being driven by massive private capital and competitive pressure between companies and nations. it feels like once the genie is out of the bottle, there's no \"policy\" that can just tell a trillion-dollar industry to slow down or go in a different direction. even if policy tries to intervene, wouldn't it just be trying to manage the fallout of an inevitable process rather than actually steering the ship?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
